 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic; the joke is on the disguises, never on patients, the dead or the bereaved. No body, remains or mourner is drawn: the coffins hold only bags. No weapon and no force are shown. The convicted men (Birmingham 2015-16, Rotterdam 2025) and the people arrested with the rally truck (Spain 2010) are never named on screen or in narration and are drawn ONLY as dark rim-lit silhouettes tagged NOT A LIKENESS; officers and agents are generic figures. The ambulance is a plain white van with AMBULANCE in plain type and a plain blue/amber light bar: no cross, star, crest or real ambulance service's livery. The rally truck carries plain RALLY lettering and generic stripes, no event or sponsor logo. The patrol car is unmarked; every plate is blank. Frame 1's scrapyard is an illustration of the reported scene, not a photograph. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue or quotation card. Facts verified 2026-10-19.",
